{% extends "layouts/app-layout.njk" %}

{% set pageTitle = "Contribution criteria" %}
{% set pageSection = "Community and contribution" %}
{% set pageDescription = "Follow these criteria when proposing a new component or pattern." %}
{% set dateUpdated = "August 2026" %}

{% block beforeContent %}
  {% include "community-and-contribution/_breadcrumb.njk" %}
{% endblock %}

{% block bodyContent %}

  <p class="app-lede-text--sub">The contents of the service manual must be of a high quality and meet user needs. To guarantee this, the service manual team checks that all components and patterns meet certain criteria.</p>

  <h2>Criteria for proposals for new components and patterns</h2>
  <p>To be successful, your proposal needs to show that the component or pattern you're suggesting will be useful and unique.</p>

  {% set proposalUsefulHtml %}
    <p>You have evidence that the component or pattern would be useful for many NHS digital teams or services.</p>
    <p>Evidence could be screenshots or links to versions in different services.</p>
  {% endset %}

  {% set proposalUniqueHtml %}
    <p>We do not already have something similar in the service manual.</p>
    <p>If you're proposing that it replace an existing component or pattern, it should be better than the existing version.</p>
  {% endset %}

  {{ table({
    caption: "Component proposal criteria and descriptions",
    captionClasses: "nhsuk-u-visually-hidden",
    firstCellIsHeader: true,
    head: [
      {
        text: "Criteria"
      },
      {
        text: "Description"
      }
    ],
    rows: [
      [
        {
          text: "Useful"
        },
        {
          html: proposalUsefulHtml
        }
      ],
      [
        {
          text: "Unique"
        },
        {
          html: proposalUniqueHtml
        }
      ]
    ]
  }) }}

  <p>The service manual team checks that proposals meet these criteria before they move them to the "To do" column in the community backlog.</p>

  <h2>Criteria for publishing a component or pattern</h2>
  <p>The team checks that the component or pattern is usable, consistent, versatile and clinically safe.</p>

  {% set publishingUsableHtml %}
    <p>You have tested it in user research and shown that it works with a representative sample of users, including people with disabilities.</p>
    <p>If there is not enough research yet to show that it's usable, it can still be published as "experimental". But it must be clearly based on relevant user research from other organisations and best practice, and meet the other criteria.</p>
  {% endset %}

  {% set publishingConsistentHtml %}
    <p>It uses existing <a href="/design-system">design system</a> styles and components where relevant.</p>
    <p>The guidance and any content in examples follow the <a href="/content">content guide</a>.</p>
    <p>If there is code, it follows <a href="https://github.com/nhsuk/nhsuk-frontend/blob/main/docs/contributing/coding-standards.md">the NHS.UK frontend coding standards in GitHub</a> and is ready to merge into the NHS.UK frontend library.</p>
  {% endset %}

  {% set publishingVersatileHtml %}
    <p>The component or pattern is versatile enough to be used in a range of different services.</p>
    <p>For example, a versatile date input component could be set up to ask for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>a year only</li>
      <li>a month and year only</li>
      <li>a precise date</li>
      <li>any other combination</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The component or pattern has been tested and works with a range of browsers, assistive technologies and devices.</p>
  {% endset %}

  {% set publishingClinicallySafeHtml %}
    <p>Where appropriate, you have involved a clinician in the design of the component or pattern and have addressed any clinical safety issues they raised.</p>
    <p>To manage clinical safety risks, the service manual team may ask you to get approval from a clinician trained in clinical safety or we may ask for advice from another clinician before approving a component or pattern.</p>
  {% endset %}

  {{ table({
    caption: "Component publishing criteria and descriptions",
    captionClasses: "nhsuk-u-visually-hidden",
    firstCellIsHeader: true,
    head: [
      {
        text: "Criteria"
      },
      {
        text: "Description"
      }
    ],
    rows: [
      [
        {
          text: "Usable"
        },
        {
          html: publishingUsableHtml
        }
      ],
      [
        {
          text: "Consistent"
        },
        {
          html: publishingConsistentHtml
        }
      ],
      [
        {
          text: "Versatile"
        },
        {
          html: publishingVersatileHtml
        }
      ],
      [
        {
          text: "Clinically safe"
        },
        {
          html: publishingClinicallySafeHtml
        }
      ]
    ]
  }) }}

<p>The service manual team uses these criteria to decide if the component or pattern is ready to publish.</p>

{% endblock %}
